# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a strand calls waituntil(event); it blocks with
#         USTRAND_REASON_EVENT; when the event fires the strand resumes
#         and prints its result.
#
# defer-to: M5
#
# Reason: the reactive runtime (at(), whenever(), waituntil(), Event.new)
# is owned entirely by M5.  There is no event-wait primitive at M3.
# The USTRAND_REASON_EVENT sub-code is reserved in the state machine but
# the wiring (UEvent, watcher pool, event-queue drain → strand unblock)
# is not present.
#
# When M5 lands, implement this fixture by:
#   var e = Event.new;
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   t: { waituntil(e?); echo("fired") };
#   e!;
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "fired"
